From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a page's cursor turns with a rotated monitor

A page's own cursor image (CSS `cursor: url(...)`, such as the hand over
a Google map) showed on its side on a rotated monitor. wm::CursorLoader
turns the themed cursors for the panel (patch 0125), but a page's image
goes through content::WebCursor, which turns it only on ChromeOS.

- CursorFactory::ShowsCursorsUnturned: true on the DRM platform, where
  a CRTC shows the cursor as it is given. False elsewhere: the host
  turns the cursor.
- There, WebCursor turns the image by the panel of the cursor client's
  display, as the loader turns the themed ones. That display follows the
  pointer across monitors.
- RenderWidgetHostViewAura rebuilds a page's image when that display
  changes, so it turns as the pointer crosses onto a monitor turned
  another way.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`. DrmCursorFactory's answer has its unit test in
ozone_unittests.
